present-reasoning-blocks-after-completion

Lane: cross

Unit: present-complete-reasoning-in-tui

ChildPatch: present-reasoning-blocks-after-completion

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Present complete reasoning as readable conversation content across live execution, restored history, pagination and exports.

Requires: Unit:frontend/toggle-tool-visibility-in-compact-transcript

Provides: Publish authoritative completed reasoning in the TUI with muted source-free gutters, preserve Markdown structure and raw-reasoning visibility, deduplicate repeated blocks within each turn across responses and steers, retain reasoning independently of tool visibility, and reproject older pages and full exports with the same turn boundaries.

Boundary: Own reasoning projection and its activity, history, pagination and export consumers. Keep incomplete reasoning out of the TUI status header, preserve pending tool ownership and complete output, retain native waiting and cancellation, protect scroll/copy state and other interface modes, and do not change model generation or persisted server records.

Verification: Focused block, live/replay, legacy-status, safety-wait restoration, interleaved-tool, restore, page-boundary, row-budget, source-selection and export tests verify full content, deduplication boundaries, ordering, visibility and preserved native behavior.

CrossGroup: control-center


